5
00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:42.000
embark on their 90-minute journey back to Port Douglas. They departed St Crispin at 3.20pm, with the crew serving food and chilled beverages to their happy and relaxed guests. The boat docked at the marina at 5pm, and after everyone had departed, the crew discovered a dive bag and a plastic bag had been left on board. This wasn't unusual, as passengers often left belongings behind by accident. The bags were set safely aside, with the expectation they would soon be claimed by their rightful owners.
开始他们返回道格拉斯港的90分钟航程。他们于下午3点20分离开圣克里斯pin礁，船员们为快乐放松的客人们提供食物和冰镇饮料。船于下午5点停靠在码头，在所有人都离开后，船员们发现船上遗留了一个潜水包和一个塑料袋。这并不罕见，因为乘客经常不小心落下随身物品。这些包被安全地放在一边，预计其失主很快就会来认领。

6
00:03:42.000 --> 00:04:23.000
The following day of Monday, January 26, a 17-year-old Outer Edge crew member was working on another tour when he came across six loose diving wets on a seabed not far from St Crispin Reef. Wets are worn by divers to counteract the buoyancy of their bodies and diving equipment, making it easier to move around underwater and remain submerged. It was odd for so many wets to be lost in such a remote location, but the crew member didn't think much of it and returned the items to the company. Co-owner Jack Nann called the find a bonus.
第二天，即1月26日星期一，“Outer Edge”的一名17岁船员正在执行另一趟旅游任务，他在距离圣克里斯pin礁不远的海床上发现了6件散落的潜水服（wets）。潜水员穿着潜水服是为了抵消身体和潜水装备的浮力，从而更容易在水下移动并保持下沉。在如此偏远的地点丢失这么多潜水服很不寻常，但该船员并没有多想，便将物品交还给了公司。联合创始人杰克·纳恩（Jack Nann）称这次发现是一笔意外之财。

7
00:04:23.000 --> 00:05:05.000
At 7pm on Tuesday, January 27, Nann noticed that the bags that had been left behind two days prior still hadn't been claimed. He peered inside the dive bag, discovering it contained a wallet, some papers, a t-shirt and dye glasses, while the plastic bag contained more clothing. The owner's diving equipment, including snorkels, wetsuits and fins, were nowhere to be seen. Nann then checked the inventory and realized that two rental air tanks were also unaccounted for. Feeling like he had, quote, been hit by a ton of bricks, Nann called another crew member
1月27日星期星期二晚上7点，纳恩注意到两天前遗留的包仍然无人认领。他往潜水包里看了看，发现里面有一个钱包、一些文件、一件T恤和潜水镜，而塑料包里则有更多衣物。失主的潜水设备，包括浮潜呼吸管、潜水服和脚蹼，却不见踪影。纳恩随后检查了库存，发现还有两个租赁气瓶下落不明。纳恩感觉自己像是被“一吨重的砖头砸中”，于是打电话给另一名船员，

8
00:05:05.000 --> 00:06:03.000
and said, I'm concerned that we may have left two divers on the reef. It looks really sus. News of the concerning discovery spread to other crew members, prompting them to gather at the Outer Edge offices to discuss the matter. Jack Nann had arranged the unclaimed contents of the diving bag on a couch and kept repeating to his staff. This is all very sus.
并说道：“我担心我们可能把两名潜水员遗忘在珊瑚礁上了。这看起来非常可疑。”这一令人担忧的发现的消息传到了其他船员那里，促使他们聚集在“Outer Edge”办公室讨论此事。杰克·纳恩将潜水包里无人认领的物品摆放在沙发上，并不断对员工们重复：“这一切都非常可疑。”

9
00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:43.000
The wallet identified the items as belonging to an American couple, 33-year-old Tom Lonergan and his 28-year-old wife, Ileane. Their shoes were still in the racks at the dock, and staff recognized the clothing as having been worn by the couple prior to them changing into their wetsuits. Dive companies were required to keep details about all their passengers, including the addresses of where they were staying, and the Lonergan's accommodation was listed as the Walk About Hostel in Cairns. Nann called the hostel and inquired about the couple, only to be told they hadn't been
钱包上的信息表明这些物品属于一对美国夫妇，33岁的汤姆·洛纳根（Tom Lonergan）和他的28岁妻子伊琳（Ileane）。他们的鞋子仍然放在码头的鞋架上，员工们认出这些衣物是这对夫妇换上潜水服之前穿的。潜水公司被要求保留所有乘客的详细信息，包括他们入住的地址，而洛纳根夫妇的住址登记在凯恩斯的“Walk About Hostel”青年旅舍。纳恩打电话到旅舍询问这对夫妇的情况，却被告知他们自两天前出发去大堡礁潜水后就再也没有露面。

10
00:06:43.000 --> 00:07:24.000
seen since leaving on their diving trip to the Great Barrier Reef two days earlier. Tom and Ileane met and fell in love while attending Louisiana State University in their hometown of Baton Rouge. They had a lot in common, both were raised in Catholic families and were dedicated students. They shared a love for the outdoors and enjoyed spending time together hiking and camping, with their families describing them as inseparable. In college, they both joined the Air Force Reserve Officer Training Corps, and after graduating they moved to Jefferson, Texas, where Tom got a job as a chemical engineer
汤姆和伊琳在他们家乡巴吞鲁日（Baton Rouge）的路易斯安那州立大学就读时相识并坠入爱河。他们有很多共同点，两人都在天主教家庭长大，并且都是刻苦的学生。他们有着对大自然的共同热爱，喜欢一起远足和露营，他们的家人形容他们形影不离。在大学里，他们都加入了空军预备役军官训练团，毕业后搬到了得克萨斯州的杰斐逊，汤姆在那里找到了一份空军化学工程师的工作，

11
