for the Air Force, while Ileane began working as a teacher. On June 24, 1988, they surprised their friends and family by eloping quietly in a private ceremony. Seven years later, in 1995, they fulfilled a lifelong dream of Ileane's by volunteering as teachers for the United States Peace Corps. They moved to the South Pacific Island nation of Tuvalu, where they lived without electricity or a telephone. Food and mail was delivered by boat once every six weeks, and although the work and the lifestyle
而伊琳则开始当老师。1988年6月24日，他们在私密仪式上悄悄私奔，给了亲友们一个惊喜。七年后的1995年，他们通过作为美国和平队（Peace Corps）的志愿者教师，实现了伊琳一生的梦想。他们搬到了南太平洋岛国图瓦卢，那里的生活没有电也没有电话。食物和邮件每六周由船只送达一次，尽管工作和生活方式极具挑战性，这对夫妇还是欣然接受了这场冒险。

12
