was challenging, the couple embraced the adventure. They were both passionate scuba divers, with over 80 dives each on their record, and they took to the waters whenever conditions were right. They loved learning about coral and fish, with their most unforgettable dive occurring in Fiji in 1997, when they swam with whales. Tom wrote about the experience in his personal diary, stating, �None of our other dives have been comparable. I just hope now that we haven't been spoiled.�
他们都是充满热情的深潜爱好者，各自的履历上有超过80次的潜水记录，只要条件合适，他们就会下水。他们喜欢了解珊瑚和鱼类，他们最难忘的一次潜水发生在1997年的斐济，当时他们与鲸鱼一起畅游。汤姆在他的个人日记中写下了这段经历：“我们的其他潜水经历都无法与之相比。我只希望现在我们还没有被宠坏。”

13
00:08:42.000 --> 00:09:25.000
After completing their two-year stint in the Peace Corps, the Lonegans planned to return to the United States and move to Hawaii, so that Tom could study marine biology. They decided to spend three months traveling around the world beforehand, visiting Australia, Indonesia and France, stopping at some of the world's best diving spots along the way. Queensland was their first destination, and they arrived in Cairns on January 15, 1998, where they checked in to the Walkabout Hostel. They were eager to go diving right away, but tropical storms had stirred up the sea, resulting in murky waters.
在完成和平队为期两年的任期后，洛纳根夫妇计划返回美国并搬到夏威夷，以便汤姆能够学习海洋生物学。在此之前，他们决定花三个月时间环游世界，访问澳大利亚、Indonesia和法国，并在途中经停一些世界上最好的潜水胜地。昆士兰是他们的第一站，他们于1998年1月15日抵达凯恩斯，并入住“Walkabout Hostel”旅舍。他们渴望立即去潜水，但热带风暴搅动了海水，导致水质浑浊。

14
00:09:25.000 --> 00:10:02.000
The Lonegans attempted one dive, but were dissatisfied with the conditions, and decided to extend their stay in the hope that the weather would improve. When the water finally cleared up, they booked a trip through the Outer Edge dive company, and on the morning of Sunday, January 25, they caught a bus to the Port Douglas Marina for the boat's 830 departure. On each boat, a member of staff was designated the role of Divemaster. It was their job to maintain a written log of when each diver entered and exited the water.
洛纳根夫妇尝试过一次潜水，但对水质条件不满意，于是决定延长停留时间，希望天气能有所改善。当海水终于变清后，他们通过“Outer Edge”潜水公司预订了一次行程。1月25日星期日早晨，他们乘坐巴士前往道格拉斯港码头，赶乘该船8点30分的出发航班。在每艘船上，都会指定一名员工担任“潜水长”（Divemaster）。他们的工作是保存一份书面日志，记录每位潜水员何时下水和出水。

15
00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:45.000
The role of Divemaster for the Lonegans trip had been assigned to Cathy Traverso, but it wasn't unusual for crew members to swap jobs throughout the day. Records taken on January 25 showed that at the first two dive sites, Tom and Dyleen had been 10 to 15 minutes late to return to the boat. At the voyage's final destination of St. Crispin, they were recorded in the logbook as entering the water at 2.20pm, around the same time as everyone else, but there was no record of them returning to the boat. It was the skipper's responsibility to do a final head count after each dive to keep
洛纳根夫妇这次行程的潜水长职责分配给了凯西·特拉韦索（Cathy Traverso），但船员在一天中互换工作并不罕见。1月25日的记录显示，在前两个潜水点，汤姆和戴琳（Dyleen）比返回船上的时间晚了10到15分钟。在航行的最后一站圣克里斯pin礁，日志记录他们于下午2点20分下水，大约和所有人同时，但没有他们返回船上的记录。每次潜水后进行最后一次清点人数以追踪船上乘客数量是船长的责任，但目前尚不清楚这是否确实发生了。

16
00:10:45.000 --> 00:11:27.000
track of the number of passengers aboard, but it was unclear exactly whether this had occurred. This realisation two days later sparked immediate fears for the couple's safety. After identifying Tom and Dyleen's abandoned belongings on Tuesday, January 27, Jack and Ian notified the police at 8.15pm, who arrived at the Outer Edge offices shortly after. Senior Constable Steve Burgess assembled the panicked staff and told them, Now is not the time to protect your backsides. Two people's lives may depend on what you tell me.
两天后的这一 realization 立即引发了对这对夫妇安全的担忧。在1月27日星期二确认了汤姆和戴琳遗弃的物品后，杰克和伊恩于晚上8点15分报警，警察不久后抵达“Outer Edge”办公室。高级警员史蒂夫·伯吉斯（Steve Burgess）集合了惊慌失措的员工并告诉他们：“现在不是推卸责任的时候。两个人的生命可能取决于你们对我说的话。”

17
00:11:27.000 --> 00:12:07.000
Honesty is the best policy. Regulations required that all scuba divers be isolated into different groups based on experience with a separate group for snorkelers. The crew recalled that Tom and Dyleen had turned down an instructor and had instead requested to dive together as a buddy team. Given they were experienced and competent divers, they were given permission to do so. Unlike most of the other divers who adopted to enter the warm waters of St Crispin Reef in nothing but their swimsuits, the couple had chosen to wear full 5mm thick wetsuits,
“诚实是上策。”规定要求所有水肺潜水员根据经验被隔离到不同的组中，浮潜者则单独成组。船员回忆说，汤姆和戴琳拒绝了教练，并要求作为潜水伴侣组一起潜水。鉴于他们是有经验且胜任的潜水员，他们得到了允许。与大多数其他潜水员选择只穿泳衣进入圣克里斯pin礁温暖水域不同，这对夫妇选择穿厚达5毫米的全套潜水服、手套和帽子，并且每人都携带了一个含有60分钟供气量的气瓶下水。

18
00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:44.000
gloves and caps, and had each entered the water carrying a tank containing 60 minutes of air supply. When the boat prepared to leave at 3pm, none of the crew recalled seeing anyone left behind in the water, nor were any micro-bubbles which are released by submerged divers visible on the surface. Micro-bubbles could typically be seen within 200 feet of the reef, and the Lonegans weren't expected to have swam any further than that. The boat was anchored only 10 feet off the reef, and at the end of the expedition, diving
当船准备在下午3点离开时，没有船员回忆看到任何人被遗留在水中，水面上也没有由水下潜水员释放的微小气泡。微小气泡通常在距离珊瑚礁200英尺的范围内可见，而洛纳根夫妇预计不会游得比这更远。船只仅在距离珊瑚礁10至15英尺处抛锚，在探险结束时，潜水教练卡尔·杰扎诺夫斯基（Carl Jezanowski）亲自清理了锚，以避免损坏珊瑚礁。据他所知，他是当天最后一个出水的人。

19
00:12:44.000 --> 00:13:25.000
instructor Carl Jezanowski had cleared the anchor himself to avoid damaging the reef. As far as he was aware, he was the last person to exit the water that day. Carl said the boat's engine had run idle for 10 minutes, with the exhausts clearly visible underwater. Even if the Lonegans had swam in the wrong direction, this alone should have alerted them to return, although Carl admitted they may not have been able to hear the engine, as the sound may have been masked by the reef. Police asked the crew whose responsibility it was to maintain the passenger lock.
卡尔说，船的发动机怠转了10分钟，排气管在水下清晰可见。即使洛纳根夫妇游错了方向，单凭这一点也应该提醒他们返回，尽管卡尔承认他们可能听不到发动机的声音，因为声音可能被珊瑚礁掩盖了。警察询问船员谁负责维护乘客名单。

20
00:13:25.000 --> 00:14:13.000
Cathy Traverso, who acted as divemaster on the day of the trip, said it was the responsibility of diving instructor Harold Closer. Harold agreed, but said Cathy also had a responsibility as she had taken the last dive for the day. Cathy was unsure whether the Lonegans returned to the boat, recalling, I thought I remembered somebody, I didn't focus, I just can't remember. The boat's manifest recorded 26 passengers, when asked if a headcount had been conducted before returning to shore, Harold Closer said, I think someone might have done one, I'm just not sure.
担任当天行程潜水长的凯西·特拉韦索表示，这是潜水教练哈罗德·克洛瑟（Harold Closer）的责任。哈罗德表示同意，但也表示凯西也有责任，因为她进行了当天的最后一次潜水。凯西不确定洛纳根夫妇是否返回了船上，她回忆说：“我以为我记得某个人，我没有集中注意力，我就是记不清了。”船只的乘客名单记录了26名乘客，当被问及在返回岸边之前是否进行了清点人数时，哈罗德·克洛瑟说：“我想有人可能做过一次，我只是不确定。”

21
